  "description": "Duoming Zhou discovered race conditions in the AX.25 amateur radio protocol\nimplementation in the Linux kernel, leading to use-after-free\nvulnerabilities. A local attacker could possibly use this to cause a denial\nof service (system crash). (CVE-2022-1205)\n\nSeveral security issues were discovered in the Linux kernel.\nAn attacker could possibly use these to compromise the system.\nThis update corrects flaws in the following subsystems:\n  - USB Gadget drivers;\n  - ARM32 architecture;\n  - ARM64 architecture;\n  - OpenRISC architecture;\n  - PowerPC architecture;\n  - RISC-V architecture;\n  - S390 architecture;\n  - x86 architecture;\n  - Block layer subsystem;\n  - Speakup Console Speech Driver;\n  - ACPI drivers;\n  - Serial ATA and Parallel ATA drivers;\n  - Auxiliary display drivers;\n  - Drivers core;\n  - Bluetooth drivers;\n  - Character device driver;\n  - TPM device driver;\n  - Clock framework and drivers;\n  - Clocksource drivers;\n  - CPU frequency scaling framework;\n  - Hardware crypto device drivers;\n  - DMA engine subsystem;\n  - EDAC drivers;\n  - Google firmware drivers;\n  - FPGA Framework;\n  - GPIO subsystem;\n  - GPU drivers;\n  - HID subsystem;\n  - HSI subsystem;\n  - Hardware monitoring drivers;\n  - CoreSight HW tracing drivers;\n  - I2C subsystem;\n  - I3C subsystem;\n  - IIO subsystem;\n  - InfiniBand drivers;\n  - On-Chip Interconnect management framework;\n  - IOMMU subsystem;\n  - IRQ chip drivers;\n  - Multiple devices driver;\n  - Media drivers;\n  - Analog Devices digital potentiometer driver;\n  - Broadcom VK accelerator driver;\n  - Fastrpc Driver;\n  - MMC subsystem;\n  - MTD block device drivers;\n  - Ethernet bonding driver;\n  - Network drivers;\n  - Mellanox network drivers;\n  - STMicroelectronics network drivers;\n  - MediaTek network drivers;\n  - Near Field Communication (NFC) drivers;\n  - NTB driver;\n  - NVDIMM (Non-Volatile Memory Device) drivers;\n  - NVME drivers;\n  - Device tree and open f